{"parentUuid":"adaea59e-fbab-4e6b-90b1-ae100363a833","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0121opJHXkPE1JuEwz9qYUe7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed. Verified in the installed Copilot 1.0.40 source (`changelog.json` and `app.js`):\n\n```js\nprocess.env.GITHUB_COPILOT_PROMPT_MODE_REPO_HOOKS === \"true\" &&\n  (h.warning(\"Loading repo hooks in prompt mode (GITHUB_COPILOT_PROMPT_MODE_REPO_HOOKS is set)\"),\n   await m.loadDeferredRepoHooks(p));\n```\n\nNote the strict `=== \"true\"` check — must be the literal string `\"true\"`, not `1` / `yes` / non-empty.\n\n## Full diagnosis\n\n**Cause:** Copilot CLI 1.0.40 (published 2026-05-01T13:08Z) made repo hooks opt-in for `-p`/`--prompt` mode. Our CI installs Copilot unpinned via `npm install -g @github/copilot` (`.github/workflows/e2e.yml:77`), so it picked up 1.0.40 immediately — the next E2E run after publication failed, and every run since.\n\n**Effect:** `copilot -p \"...\" --allow-all` runs but never invokes `.github/hooks/entire.json`, so no copilot lifecycle hooks fire, no shadow-branch session is initialized, no checkpoint is condensed at user-commit time. Test then waits 30s for `entire/checkpoints/v1` to advance and times out. Interactive (tmux) tests are unaffected because the gating only applies to prompt mode.\n\n**Fix options (pick one or both):**\n\n1. **Quickest** — set env in the e2e harness so existing tests pass again:\n   ```go\n   // e2e/agents/copilot-cli.go:77\n   cmd.Env = append(os.Environ(),\n       \"ENTIRE_TEST_TTY=0\",\n       \"GITHUB_COPILOT_PROMPT_MODE_REPO_HOOKS=true\",\n   )\n   ```\n   Same for the summary-gen invocation at `copilot-cli.go:300`. Production summary-gen at `cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go:17` also needs `GITHUB_COPILOT_PROMPT_MODE_REPO_HOOKS=true` if it shells out via `-p` (worth checking — that path uses stdin pipe, but I'd verify it isn't also gated).\n\n2. **Defensive** — pin Copilot